[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m To solve this problem, let's denote the number of coins in each of the seven original bags as \( x \). After finding a bag of 53 coins, the total number of coins becomes \( 7x + 53 \). After redistributing these coins evenly into eight bags, each bag will contain \( \frac{7x + 53}{8} \) coins. According to the problem, this value is equal to the number of coins in each of the original seven bags, so we have:
