[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m To solve this problem, we need to determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that includes at least one member from each party (Republican and Democrat). We will use the principle of complementary counting, which involves subtracting the number of invalid subcommittees (those that do not include members from both parties) from the total number of possible subcommittees.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m ### Step 1: Calculate the total number of ways to choose 5 members from 14
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m The total number of ways to choose 5 members from 14 is given by the combination formula \( \binom{n}{k} \), which represents the number of ways to choose \( k \) items from \( n \) items without regard to order.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5! \cdot 9!}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m Calculating this, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m ### Step 2: Calculate the number of ways to choose 5 members that are all Republicans
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m If all 5 members are Republicans, we choose 5 out of 8. This is given by \( \binom{8}{5} \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8!}{5! \cdot 3!} = \frac{8 \times 7 \times 6}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m ### Step 3: Calculate the number of ways to choose 5 members that are all Democrats
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m If all 5 members are Democrats, we choose 5 out of 6. This is given by \( \binom{6}{5} \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6!}{5! \cdot 1!} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m ### Step 4: Calculate the number of invalid subcommittees
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m The number of invalid subcommittees (those that do not include members from both parties) is the sum of the invalid subcommittees of all Republicans and all Democrats.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \binom{8}{5} + \binom{6}{5} = 56 + 6 = 62
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m ### Step 5: Calculate the number of valid subcommittees
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m The number of valid subcommittees is the total number of subcommittees minus the number of invalid subcommittees.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 2002 - 62 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m Therefore, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party is:
