[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m    - We need this to be more than 200:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m      56m - 21 > 200
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m      56m > 221
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m      m > \frac{221}{56} \approx 3.946
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m    - The smallest integer \( m \) that satisfies this is \( m = 4 \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 6. **Calculate the Total Number of Coins:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m    - Substitute \( m = 4 \) into the expression for the total number of coins:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m      \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m      56m - 21 = 56 \cdot 4 - 21 = 224 - 21 = 203
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m      \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m Therefore, the smallest number of coins you could have had before finding the bag of 53 coins is \(\boxed{203}\).
