[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m To solve this problem, we need to determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee of 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, ensuring that the subcommittee has at least one member from each party. We will use the principle of complementary counting to simplify the process.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m First, we calculate the total number of ways to choose 5 members from the 14 available members (8 Republicans and 6 Democrats):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5! \cdot 9!} = 2002
