[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members with at least one member from each party, we can use the principle of complementary counting. This involves calculating the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members and then subtracting the number of ways to form a subcommittee that is entirely from one party.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m First, calculate the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from the 14 members (8 Republicans + 6 Democrats):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5! \cdot 9!} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m Next, calculate the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that is entirely from one party. There are two cases to consider: entirely from Republicans or entirely from Democrats.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 1. Subcommittee of 5 members entirely from Republicans:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8!}{5! \cdot 3!} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 2. Subcommittee of 5 members entirely from Democrats:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6!}{5! \cdot 1!} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m Adding these two cases together gives the total number of ways to form a subcommittee that is entirely from one party:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 56 + 6 = 62
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m Finally, subtract the number of subcommittees that are entirely from one party from the total number of subcommittees:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 2002 - 62 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
