[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m The numbers are 7, 2, \( x \), and 10.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m The arithmetic mean is 9.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m The formula for the arithmetic mean is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \text{Arithmetic Mean} = \frac{\text{Sum of the numbers}}{\text{Count of the numbers}}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m Here, the count of the numbers is 4. So, the arithmetic mean is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 9 = \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4}
