[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \text{Arithmetic Mean} = \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m We know that the arithmetic mean is 9, so we can set up the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 9 = \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m First, simplify the numerator on the right side of the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 9 = \frac{19 + x}{4}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m To eliminate the fraction, multiply both sides of the equation by 4:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 9 \cdot 4 = 19 + x
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
