[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m To solve this problem, we need to determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee that has 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, ensuring that the subcommittee has at least one member from each party.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m First, we calculate the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from the 14 members (8 Republicans + 6 Democrats). This can be done using the combination formula \( \binom{n}{k} \), which represents the number of ways to choose \( k \) items from \( n \) items without regard to the order of selection.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m The total number of ways to choose 5 members from 14 members is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5! \cdot 9!}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m Calculating this, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12 \times 11 \times 10}{5 \times 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m Next, we need to subtract the number of subcommittees that do not have any members from either party. There are two such subcommittees: one that consists entirely of Republicans and one that consists entirely of Democrats.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m The number of ways to choose 5 members from 8 Republicans is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8!}{5! \cdot 3!} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m The number of ways to choose 5 members from 6 Democrats is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6!}{5! \cdot 1!} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m Adding these two results gives the total number of invalid subcommittees:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 56 + 6 = 62
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m Finally, we subtract the number of invalid subcommittees from the total number of possible subcommittees to get the number of valid subcommittees with at least one member from each party:
