[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m To solve this problem, we need to determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee consisting of 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, such that the subcommittee includes at least one member from each party.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1952501)[0m First, we will calculate the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from the 14 available members (8 Republicans + 6 Democrats). This is given by the combination formula \(\binom{n}{k}\), which represents the number of ways to choose \(k\) items from \(n\) items without regard to the order of selection.
